+visual selection yanks, rendering invalidation, and polling background workers. Insert mode sends
+chat text to the selected agent session, or to `command-agent` when the Work Leaf command surface is
+selected. Bracketed-paste newlines and Shift+Enter are chat prompt line breaks. A plain Enter submits
+the buffered chat text. When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds
+the chat buffer with `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same
+selected-agent chat path. Selected-agent slash input is displayed in the chat transcript and reaches
+the active backend through its command-execution hook instead of the normal prompt-send hook.
+
+Command mode supports Vim-style visual selection in the focused pane. `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V` start
+character, line, and block visual selections; cursor movement extends the selection; `y` yanks the
+selected text; and `Y` starts a line selection and yanks it. Visual selection works in both the agent
+list and the transcript pane, and right-pane selections use the same wrapped rows that the renderer
+shows on screen.
 
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
 state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
@@ -309,7 +315,8 @@ again.
